Notes: THE SATURATING CEILING of the plasma glucose to plasma insulin relation, derived from Merovci 2021's two second-phase clamp plateaux. 139 mU/L = 966 pmol/L, entered at two figures as 970. || THE SOURCE IS A TWO-STEP HYPERGLYCAEMIC CLAMP IN 12 HEALTHY SUBJECTS with no family history of type 2 diabetes, and what is taken is the BASELINE arm, before the 72-hour glucose infusion. The post-infusion arm is an intervention and glucose_insulin_prereg.md section 12.4 excludes it for setting a healthy relation. || THE PROTOCOL COMES FROM THE METHODS AND NOT THE ABSTRACT, and the difference matters: the abstract's '100 and 300 mg/dL' are INCREMENTS, while the methods give step one as 100 mg/dL above baseline and step two as 400 mg/dL ABSOLUTE. Second-phase insulin is an incremental AUC over 70-minute windows, so the plateau concentrations are those AUCs divided by 70 and added to fasting: 9 mU/L at 5.00 mmol/L, 42 at 10.55, 78 at 22.20. || AN EXACT TWO-POINT INVERSION, NOT A FIT. Two parameters from two increments reproduce both points identically, so there is NO goodness of fit and no residual - the form is interpolation between two measured points and extrapolation beyond them. || UNCERTAINTY IS LARGE AND IS WHY ONLY TWO FIGURES ARE ENTERED. The two AUCs carry SE of 21 and 24 percent, and the inversion is sensitive to their ratio, so these constants are known to tens of percent at best. Directive 1.13. || SE, NOT SD: the AUC dispersions are standard errors over n = 12, so thirst_prereg.md section 8.4's conversion applies to any population sampling of this relation. || SINGLE-SOURCE, AND IT SAYS SO. A second two-step hyperglycaemic clamp in healthy adults reporting both axes would pool with this one; OPEN-QUESTIONS B21 carries the debt. || IT IS AN EXTRAPOLATION BEYOND THE DATA. Merovci's highest step is 22.2 mmol/L; this ceiling is what the two-point form implies as glucose goes to infinity, and no measurement constrains it there. The model reaches about 29 mmol/L, so