"""Concentration-independent share of non-insulin-mediated glucose uptake at fasting glucose [unitless] +/- 0.34 (sd)
Source (tier A, derived): Baron AD, Brechtel G, Wallace P, Edelman SV. Rates of noninsulin-mediated glucose uptake are elevated in type II diabetic subjects. J Clin Invest 1985;76(5):1782-1788. PMID 2865274. Full text read. Corroborated on the FORM, not pooled, by Best JD, Taborsky GJ, Halter JB, Porte D. Glucose disposal is not proportional to plasma glucose level in man. Diabetes 1981;30(10):847-850. PMID 6115785.
Notes: THE CONCENTRATION-INDEPENDENT SHARE OF NON-INSULIN-MEDIATED GLUCOSE UPTAKE, at the fasting glucose level. OPEN-QUESTIONS B22; pre-registered in validation/nimgu_form_prereg.md, branch N1; ADR 0033. || WHY IT EXISTS. ADR 0031 made NIMGU strictly proportional to glucose, k_ni*G, and said so: with both disease knobs at zero the insulin-independent term alone cleared the whole appearance at 15.6 mmol/L, below the renal threshold, so glycosuria was zero at every setting. ADR 0031 named its own falsifier and deferred the fix rather than stacking a second structural change. This is that fix. || THE FORM IS BEST 1981'S STATED MECHANISM, NOT A CURVE FIT: insulin-independent tissues such as brain have a relatively fixed glucose uptake while other tissues take up glucose at a rate proportional to concentration. So NIMGU = U_fixed + k_ni*G, two terms, one new parameter. || THE VALUE IS AN EXACT TWO-POINT INVERSION OF BARON 1985, FULL TEXT READ (open access at JCI, downloaded from the publisher's own open-access link; no bot check was involved or circumvented). Table I gives control fasting serum glucose 90 +/- 1.7 mg/dl, n = 11. NIMGU was 113 +/- 8 mg/min at euglycaemia (n = 11) and 186 +/- 19 mg/min at a somatostatin + hyperglycaemic clamp of 248 +/- 2 mg/dl (n = 7 - only seven controls underwent the hyperglycaemic arm, which the abstract does not say). k_ni = (186-113)/(248-90) = 0.462 (mg/min)/(mg/dl); U_fixed = 113 - 0.462*90 = 71.4 mg/min; fraction = 71.4/113 = 0.63. TWO POINTS, TWO PARAMETERS: an exact inversion, no residual and no goodness of fit. || THE PAPER CONTAINS ITS OWN CONSISTENCY CHECK AND THE FIT PASSES IT. It separately reports NIMGU metabolic clearance falling 1.2 +/- 0.07 to 0.74 +/- 0.08; the fitted rates give 113/90 = 1.256 and 186/248 = 0.750. The rates and the clearances are one dataset, not two claims. THE CLEARANCE FALL IS 38 PERCENT FROM THE PRINTED CLEARANCES AND 40 PERCENT FROM THE FITTED RATES; those are two-figure numbers whose ratio carries several points of uncertainty and directive 1.13 forbids reading a difference inside that as anything. NEITHER MAY BE QUOTED TO THREE FIGURES. || INDEPENDENT CORROBORATION, AND IT IS WHY THIS ROW EXISTS AT ALL UNDER DIRECTIVE 1.16. Best JD, Taborsky GJ, Halter JB, Porte D. Glucose disposal is not proportional to plasma glucose level in man. Diabetes 1981;30(10):847-850, PMID 6115785 - a DIFFERENT laboratory (Porte, Seattle), decade and protocol (somatostatin at three fixed insulin levels), reporting metabolic clearance falling 38 percent at low insulin. Its implied concentration-independent fraction is 63 to 76 percent and CONTAINS Baron's 63. NOT POOLED: its abstract says only 'more than twice basal', which spans 63 at 2.5x and 76 at 2.0x, so it corroborates the FORM and cannot supply a value. Found through the reference list of Ahren and Pacini, J Diabetes Investig 2021, PMID 33098240 - it uses the term NIMGU nowhere and no search on that term returns it. || THE REVIEW MISCITED IT as Diabetes 1981;34:847-850; volume 34 is 1985. Verified against the indexed record. Directive 1.5. || DISPERSION. Baron reports SEM throughout. SD propagated from the two arms with their own n: 113 +/- 8 (n=11) gives SD 26.5 and 186 +/- 19 (n=7) gives SD 50.3, so the fraction carries SD 0.34. THAT IS AN UPPER BOUND AND IS LABELLED ONE: the propagation assumes the two arms are INDEPENDENT and they are not - seven of the eleven controls appear in both - so the true between-subject spread is smaller and cannot be computed without subject-level data. A population model needs the spread and this is the honest ceiling on it. || WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. That the two-term form beats a saturating Michaelis form on DATA. Two points cannot distinguish them; the choice is on Best's stated mechanism, and nimgu_form_prereg.md section 7 test 5 declared the comparison in advance. Edelman 1990 (PMID 1973673, closed) has a FOUR-point dose-response and would decide it. || SCALING: none, a fraction.
"""
const GLU_NIMGU_FIXED_FRACTION = 0.63

