"""Vagal chronotropic effector time constant [s] +/- 0.2-0.6 (range)
Source (tier A, reported): La Rovere MT, Pinna GD, Raczak G. Baroreflex sensitivity: measurement and clinical implications. Ann Noninvasive Electrocardiol 2008;13(2):191-207.
Notes: ADDED 2026-09-08 BECAUSE THE MODEL DEMANDED IT, NOT BECAUSE THE PRE-REGISTRATION WANTED IT. validation/chronotropic_baroreflex_prereg.md section 5 made the chronotropic arm ALGEBRAIC by default and put the burden on ADDING a lag, on the directive 1.10 grounds that a 200-600 ms effector is quasi-static against a six-hour protocol. THAT WAS REFUTED BY BUILDING IT. || WHY. An algebraic hr_mod closes an INSTANTANEOUS ALGEBRAIC LOOP through arterial pressure: cardiac output sets MAP, MAP sets the baroreflex error, the error sets heart rate, and heart rate sets cardiac output. structural_simplify resolved it by promoting Blood.CO to a state - so the 'stateless' arm cost a state anyway, in another component, where it meant nothing. The vasomotor arm never had this problem because BR.EFFECTOR.TAU makes tpr_mod a STATE, and a lag is exactly what breaks an algebraic loop. || SO THE STATE IS PAID FOR EITHER WAY AND THIS IS THE HONEST PLACE TO PUT IT: on a variable with a physical meaning and a sourced time constant, rather than on an implicit nonlinear unknown inside the blood component. Ten states before, eleven after, and the eleventh is br.hr_mod. || THE VALUE. La Rovere reports the parasympathetic limb of the baroreflex acting on heart rate in 200-600 ms, against 2-3 s for the sympathetic vasomotor limb - the same sentence BR.EFFECTOR.TAU is entered from, and the reason ADR 0009 gave for lumping the arms in the first place. 0.4 s is the midpoint of that reported range, entered the same way BR.EFFECTOR.TAU takes 3.0 from 2.0-3.0. THE RANGE IS THE UNCERTAINTY AND IT IS THREEFOLD. || IT IS SEVEN TIMES FASTER THAN THE VASOMOTOR EFFECTOR, which is the physiology: vagal transmission is fast and cholinergic, sympathetic vasomotor transmission is slow and noradrenergic. That ratio is now the smallest declared time constant in the model and it widens the stiffness range - 0.4 s against a 10.3 day thyroxine turnover is about 2.2 million. ADR 0003 stays deferred on state count