Source (tier B, reported): Yamasaki F, Sato T, Sato K, Diedrich A. Analytic and integrative framework for understanding human sympathetic arterial baroreflex function. Front Neurosci 2021;15:707345.
Notes: 2.0 -> 5.62 ON 2026-09-09, AT THE OWNER'S EXPLICIT INSTRUCTION, AND THE CITATION DID NOT CHANGE. That is the whole point of this row's history: it cited Yamasaki 2021 the entire time and carried a number from his INTRODUCTION instead of his RESULT. || WHAT IT WAS. 2.0, the mid-point of an ANIMAL range of 1.0-3.5 that Yamasaki cites in his introduction from Kent 1972, Shoukas and Sagawa 1973, McRitchie 1976, Burattini 1994, Sato 1999 and Sunagawa 2001 - isolated carotid sinus or aortic arch perfusion in dog and rabbit. The note also repeated his sentence that the invasive approach is not applicable to humans and that human open-loop gain HAS NOT BEEN CLARIFIED. || THAT SENTENCE IS THE PAPER'S PROBLEM STATEMENT AND THE PAPER IS THE ANSWER TO IT. Yamasaki F, Sato T, Sato K, Diedrich A. Front Neurosci 2021;15:707345, PMC8322947, OPEN ACCESS, READ IN FULL. He measured it in humans: GL(0) = 5.62 +/- 0.98 SUPINE and GL(15) = 3.75 +/- 0.62 at 15 degrees head-up tilt. Table 2, and both Methods and the table legend state 'Values are means +/- SD'. THE SUPINE VALUE IS TAKEN because supine is the posture this model means by nominal - the same reason CV.HR.NOMINAL takes the supine Fenland figure. || IT IS THE SAME QUANTITY IN THE SAME UNITS AS THE MODEL'S SLOT. GL is defined as the product of the mechanoneural and neuromechanical arcs, with ARTERIAL PRESSURE as the output variable - the ratio of an arterial pressure change to a baroreceptor pressure change, dimensionless. The addendum to ADR 0009 computes that this model's G_br is exactly that: the tanh slope at the operating point is G_br/MAP_ref and dMAP/dtpr_mod is about MAP_ref, so the product is G_br. Commensurable by definition rather than by assumption. || AND IT IS THE VAGAL-EXCLUDED GAIN, WHICH IS EXACTLY WHAT THIS ROW SHOULD NOW HOLD. Yamasaki blocked vagal effects with atropine 0.4 mg/kg in every protocol, so 5.62 is sympathetic arterial pressure control with the cardiac vagal limb removed. Since 2026-09-08 that limb is a SEPARATE effector, BR.CARDIAC.GAIN under ADR 0022, so the two rows now partition the reflex the way the measurements do. Before ADR 0022 this change would have LOST the vagal contribution entirely; after it, it is the coherent pairing. THE RESIDUAL OVERLAP IS UNCHANGED AND DECLARED: atropine removes vagal chronotropy but not cardiac sympathetic chronotropy, so a small part of the cardiac limb sits inside 5.62 as well as inside BR.CARDIAC.GAIN. || THE WEAKNESSES, AND THEY ARE REAL. n = 7. Healthy male volunteers aged 19-37. THE AUTHORS THEMSELVES DISCLAIM REPRESENTATIVENESS in their limitations: 'we could not conclude that the parameters are representative of a normal population', and they call for larger studies across ages and health statuses. It is entered `both` under ADR 0014's rule that a single supported value serves both sexes, so THIS IS A MALE NUMBER APPLIED TO WOMEN - the CV.HEMATOCRIT.NOMINAL failure exactly, declared rather than hidden. It is also a YOUNG cohort against a model whose stroke volume comes from 45-74 year olds and whose heart rate comes from 29-65, and baroreflex gain falls steeply with age. || WHY IT IS STILL BETTER THAN WHAT IT REPLACED. Seven young men measured directly beat six animal studies read through an introduction, in the right species, the right posture and the right units. The uncertainty is now a reported SD rather than the spread of somebody else's citations. || THE ETHICAL-CEILING ARGUMENT IN ADR 0009'S ADDENDUM IS FALSIFIED BY THIS SAME PAPER. That addendum tiered this row E2 on the grounds that opening the baroreflex loop is 'definitionally terminal' and so not performable in humans. Yamasaki performed it - not by isolating a carotid sinus, but by constructing an equilibrium diagram from graded tilt and ganglionic blockade, which reaches the open-loop gain without opening the loop surgically. THE QUANTITY WAS OBTAINABLE ALL ALONG BY A DIFFERENT METHOD, which is HANDOVER section 3.19's lesson repeated: that pass