e average FALL with intake. D4 says report the disagreement and do not split it. || AND THE MARGINAL FRACTION IS NOT A CLEAN MEASUREMENT OF THE DIETARY ONE: it is the fate of a potassium chloride tablet, not of food, and tablet absorption, incomplete 24-hour collections and trial compliance all push it down with the same sign. Reported because it is what was measured; not used to move this row. || THE PRODUCT OF THIS ROW AND K.INTAKE.NOMINAL IS NOW CHECKED AGAINST SOMETHING, WHICH IT NEVER WAS. 0.884 * 69.06 = 61.05 mmol/day of urinary potassium, against 61.17 measured by 24-hour collection in the 19 control arms of Cappuccio 2016 across 12 countries - 0.2 percent. TREAT THAT AS TOO GOOD: NHANES dietary recall understates intake and those cohorts are not American, so two quantities that should not agree this closely do. What it rules out is a gross error in a product that had never been compared with any measurement at all. || Urinary potassium over dietary potassium at the end of each experimental period, in the six admissible studies: 0.852, 0.974, 0.845, 1.008, 0.945, 0.681; mean 0.884. The residual is stool, which this model does not have. || THE RANGE INCLUDES A VALUE ABOVE 1, which is not an error: those subjects were in negative potassium balance during a load, still excreting stores laid down earlier. A one-compartment model cannot represent that and the range records it. || IT IS A FRACTION, SO IT IS INTENSIVE, and the intake it multiplies already scales. || TWO GOOD GROUPS DISAGREE AND IT IS NOT AVERAGED HERE. This row is a CONSTANT and the human fraction is not: Hene 1986 (PMID 3523191) measured urinary potassium 50 of 80 mEq/day, rising to 233 of 300, so 0.63 -> 0.78; Rabelink 1990 (PMID 2266680) about 0.80 at 400 mmol/day. Every Utrecht value is BELOW Brunner's 0.884 and the fraction clearly RISES WITH INTAKE, which this model cannot represent. Not pooled, because all three Utrecht numbers are abstract-level - none is open access - and averaging abstracts against a full-text extraction needs its own pre-registration. ADR 0021 amendment A7 disagreement 1.
