Notes: THE ROW ADR 0018 SAID DID NOT EXIST. Its deferral of the Fick relation read 'they need tissue oxygen consumption, which is a metabolic row this model does not have'; §3.27 built the arm from CO2 production over the exchange ratio, and this row now sources the same quantity from the measurement directly. || THE EXCHANGE RATIO BARELY MATTERS HERE, which is why an assumed 0.80 does not block it: the Weir denominator runs 4.771 at R = 0.75 to 4.881 at R = 0.85, ±1.1 percent across the whole plausible resting range. The stratum choice is eight times larger. || 228 mL/min AGAINST THE TEXTBOOK 250, and the 250 is 3.5 mL/kg/min - the metabolic-equivalent convention this source exists to refute. || IT WIDENS A DISCREPANCY RATHER THAN CLOSING ONE, and metabolic_rate_prereg.md branch M3 required that be reported: with cardiac output at 5.95 L/min the oxygen extraction ratio falls from 20.1 percent to 18.3 percent against roughly 23 percent implied by a measured mixed venous saturation near 75. The Fick-consistent cardiac output would be 4.75 L/min. That points at CV.CO.NOMINAL - derived from a CARDIAC-MRI stroke volume, where mixed venous saturation is measured against thermodilution and Fick outputs - and it is NOT closed here by choosing a different stratum. || PRECISION RAISED 2026-09-05: this is a DERIVED row closing an identity, so it carries every digit the arithmetic gives rather than the significant figures of the measurement behind it - the exemption pooling.md records, and the lesson CV.CO.NOMINAL wrote down. Rounding it to four figures put arterial PCO2 out by 1 part in 10,000, which the suite caught. The MEASUREMENT it descends from, RESP.METABOLIC_RATE, stays at the three figures its source reports. || ROUNDED 2026-09-09 TO MEASUREMENT PRECISION at the owner's instruction. Nothing physiological in this model is measured to more than four significant figures, and trailing zeros on a whole number read as precision that is not there. The discarded digits were floating-point residue from the derivation, not information. Directive 1.13.
"""
const RESP_O2_CONSUMPTION = 0.228

