"""Open-loop gain of the pituitary-thyroid feedback [dimensionless] +/- 1.793-2.761 (range)
Source (tier A, derived): Benhadi N, Fliers E, Visser TJ, Reitsma JB, Wiersinga WM. Eur J Endocrinol 2010;162(2):323-9. PMID 19926783, ABSTRACT ONLY, n = 21 healthy volunteers under randomised T4 and T3 loading - a WITHIN-SUBJECT PERTURBATION, which is the design a feedback gain needs. Reported log TSH = 1.50 - 0.059 x FT4, base 10 (see validation/thyroid_extract.py section 1). || AND Jostel A, Ryder WDJ, Shalet SM. Clin Endocrinol (Oxf) 2009;71(4):529-34. PMID 19226261, ABSTRACT ONLY, 9519 tests in 4064 patients, 0.1345 per pmol/L in natural-log units, combined with the free-thyroxine mean of the cohort that applies it in Wang Y et al. Front Endocrinol (Lausanne) 2021;12:657114, PMC8129566, OPEN ACCESS, read in full.
