Source (tier A, derived): DERIVED, and it had to become derived. b = THY.LOOP_GAIN / THY.FT4.EUTHYROID = 2.277 / 10.16, because a slope in units of 1/(pmol/L) is SCALE-DEPENDENT and the model's free thyroxine is now on the NHANES immunoassay scale. The measured slopes it comes from are on other scales and cannot be transferred directly. Sources behind the loop gain: Benhadi N, Fliers E, Visser TJ, Reitsma JB, Wiersinga WM. Eur J Endocrinol 2010;162(2):323-9. PMID 19926783, ABSTRACT ONLY, n = 21 healthy volunteers under randomised T4 and T3 loading - a WITHIN-SUBJECT PERTURBATION, which is the design a feedback gain needs. Reported log TSH = 1.50 - 0.059 x FT4, base 10 (see validation/thyroid_extract.py section 1). || AND Jostel A, Ryder WDJ, Shalet SM. Clin Endocrinol (Oxf) 2009;71(4):529-34. PMID 19226261, ABSTRACT ONLY, 9519 tests in 4064 patients, 0.1345 per pmol/L in natural-log units, combined with the free-thyroxine mean of the cohort that applies it in Wang Y et al. Front Endocrinol (Lausanne) 2021;12:657114, PMC8129566, OPEN ACCESS, read in full.
