    :AB_CO2_SOLUBILITY => Provenance("AB.CO2.SOLUBILITY", "mmol/L/mmHg", 0.03, "B", "reported", "Bellelli A. Blood buffers: the viewpoint of a biochemist. Physiol Rep 2025;13(9):e70345. PMC12051385. OPEN ACCESS, READ IN FULL. States the apparent pK of the carbon dioxide / bicarbonate pair in plasma as 6.1 at 37 degrees C, citing Ellison G, Straumfjord JV, Hummel JP. Clin Chem 1958;4(6):452-61 - WHICH WAS NOT OPENED, and directive 1.5 means this row cites what was read and names what it did not. The same review uses a carbon dioxide solubility of 0.03 mmol/L/mmHg.", "TWO SIGNIFICANT FIGURES BECAUSE THAT IS WHAT THE SOURCE CARRIES. The figure often quoted to three, 0.0301, would change arterial pH by 0.0015 - below the resolution of any blood gas analyser and far below the 0.02 the venous-to-arterial offset on AB.HCO3.PLASMA is worth. Entering the extra digit would be claiming a precision that changes nothing, which is directive 1.9. || NOT TO BE CONFUSED WITH BLOOD.O2.SOLUBILITY, which is oxygen, in mL/dL/mmHg, and a different quantity in different units."),
    :AB_HCO3_PLASMA => Provenance("AB.HCO3.PLASMA", "mmol/L", 25.04, "A", "reported", "National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey 2007-2008, 2009-2010 and 2011-2012, public microdata, file BIOPRO (standard biochemistry profile), variable LBXSC3SI. EXTRACTED HERE: validation/acid_base_extract.py. n = 8809 adults aged 20+, not pregnant, weighted with WTMEC2YR/3 for three pooled cycles. Mean 25.04 mmol/L, SD 2.24, 2.5th-97.5th percentile 20.0-29.0.", "AN INPUT, NOT AN OUTPUT, AND ADR 0020 WAS AMENDED TO SAY SO. That record planned a bicarbonate STATE with renal net acid excretion balancing endogenous acid production. Neither half could be sourced: the renal response to plasma bicarbonate exists in humans almost entirely in disease preparations (pre-registration branch A3, and directive 1.7's fifth subsystem), and net endogenous acid production on an ordinary diet spans threefold across the sources that could be opened - 22 mEq/day measured in 90 healthy omnivorous adults against a conventional 70. A balance whose input flux is uncertain threefold and whose renal gain is unsourced is a balance in which the set-point does all the work. || SO THE DEPENDENCY IS INVERTED for the third time in this model, after arterial PCO2 (ADR 0017) and the thyroid operating point (section 3.26): source the quantity that is actually measured - and plasma bicarbonate is measured in every basic metabolic panel, here in 8809 adults - and let the composed quantity be the output. || THE SCALE CAVEAT, STATED BEFORE IT BITES RATHER THAN AFTER. This is a VENOUS serum TOTAL CARBON DIOXIDE, which is what a clinical chemistry panel measures; Henderson-Hasselbalch wants ARTERIAL BICARBONATE. The two differ twice over: total CO2 includes dissolved gas and carbamino compounds as well as bicarbonate, and venous blood carries more of all of them than arterial. The combined offset is conventionally 1 to 2 mmol/L. || NO CORRECTION IS APPLIED, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. Applying one would set this parameter from arterial pH, which is the quantity the falsifiable test judges - the error that voided ADR 0019's test 2. The model therefore reports pH 7.420 against a human arterial reference near 7.40, and the 0.02 residual is the size of the unapplied offset: subtracting 1 mmol/L gives 7.402. THAT ARITHMETIC IS THE POINT - the discrepancy is explained and not closed. || This is the THIRD time a measurement-scale mismatch has mattered in this model (HANDOVER section 3.26, section 3.28, and here) and the first time it was caught before rather than after the number was believed. || SEX: no pair taken; ADR 0014's shared-value branch. The NHANES difference between the sexes is small and was not tested here."),
    :AB_PK_APPARENT => Provenance("AB.PK_APPARENT", "dimensionless", 6.1, "B", "reported", "Bellelli A. Blood buffers: the viewpoint of a biochemist. Physiol Rep 2025;13(9):e70345. PMC12051385. OPEN ACCESS, READ IN FULL. States the apparent pK of the carbon dioxide / bicarbonate pair in plasma as 6.1 at 37 degrees C, citing Ellison G, Straumfjord JV, Hummel JP. Clin Chem 1958;4(6):452-61 - WHICH WAS NOT OPENED, and directive 1.5 means this row cites what was read and names what it did not. The same review uses a carbon dioxide solubility of 0.03 mmol/L/mmHg.", "ONE OF THE ROUND NUMBERS acid_base_prereg.md section 3 listed in advance as presumptively unsourced, and it survives - but it is entered because a source states it at a stated temperature, not because it is round. || TIER B, NOT A: the value was read in a review that cites the primary measurement rather than in the primary measurement itself. SOURCES.md permits that with the flag, and the flag is this sentence. || CONDITIONS ARE PART OF THE VALUE: 37 degrees C, normal plasma ionic strength and protein. The apparent pK varies with all three, and the states where it varies most - severe acidosis, hypoalbuminaemia, hypothermia - are states this model does not represent, which is why a fixed value is admissible here and would not be in an intensive care model."),
    :ADH_OSM_SENSITIVITY => Provenance("ADH.OSM.SENSITIVITY", "1/(mOsm/kg)", 0.12, "B", "derived", "Baylis PH, Pippard C, Gill GV, Burd J. Development of a cytochemical assay for plasma vasopressin: application to studies on water loading normal man. Clin Endocrinol (Oxf) 1986;24(4):383-393.", "PRECISION: rounded to 3 significant figures on 2026-08-27. The sources do not support more, and carrying digits that do not exist forced the closure gate and the test suite to chase arithmetic noise. Derived rows inherit the significant figures of their inputs and are rounded to match; the closure tolerance was moved to 1e-3 in the same change, which is still an order of magnitude tighter than the 6% error that motivated that gate. || DERIVED, not fitted and not assumed. Forced by requiring that at the plasma osmolality setpoint the model excretes exactly intake minus insensible loss, which is what the pre-ADH placeholder did. k_adh = ((solute/(intake-insensible)) - U_min) / ((U_max - U_min) * (Osm_set - Osm_thr)) = 0.08780904 per mOsm/kg, giving antidiuretic activity 0.263427 at baseline - a quarter of maximal, with room to move both ways. Closure constraint enforced by tools/check_closure.py. THIS IS NOT ZERBE'S SENSITIVITY: that is 0.12-1.66 pg/ml per mOsm/kg and this is a normalised 0-1 activity, because no sourced map from plasma vasopressin to urine osmolality was found. || RECOMPUTED 2026-09-01, 0.0878 -> 0.10835, when ADH.URINE.OSM_MAX moved 1200 -> 982 (Tryding 1988). k_adh = ((solute/v_base) - U_min) / ((U_max - U_min) * (Osm_set - Osm_thr)) = (352.941176 - 50) / (932 * 3). The DERIVATION is unchanged and so is the operating point it pins: at the plasma osmolality setpoint the model still excretes exactly intake minus insensible loss, by construction. What changes is the SLOPE - a lower ceiling reached over the same osmolality span means each mOsm/kg buys more antidiuretic activity. Five significant figures because the closure check compares this against its own der